Python 3.10 compatibility: fall back for the two 3.11-only names.

picpro 0.4.1 declares requires-python >= 3.12, but the only 3.11-only
names it uses are importlib.resources.abc.Traversable (a submodule only
since 3.11) and typing.Self (added in 3.11). The platform runs this tool
under its own interpreter, which can be 3.10, so both fall back to their
3.10 spellings. 3.9 stays out: PEP 604 unions are used throughout without
a future import. Sent upstream so the queue can shrink.

diff --git a/picpro/bin/picpro.py b/picpro/bin/picpro.py
--- a/picpro/bin/picpro.py	2026-09-29 15:02:25.666933132 -0300
+++ b/picpro/bin/picpro.py	2026-09-29 15:02:25.730049566 -0300
@@ -50,7 +50,10 @@
 from collections.abc import Callable
 from functools import wraps
 from importlib.resources import files
-from importlib.resources.abc import Traversable
+try:
+    from importlib.resources.abc import Traversable
+except ImportError:
+    from importlib.abc import Traversable
 from pathlib import Path
 from typing import TypeVar
 
